# Server-side only (never shipped in the app bundle) — used by app/api/*+api.ts
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Server-side only. Writes the shared species catalog and the rate-limit counter,
# neither of which clients may write. Bypasses row level security, so it must
# never gain an EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix.
#
# Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API Keys → Secret keys.
# New projects issue sb_secret_... here; older ones show a service_role JWT
# starting eyJ... Either works — both bypass row level security.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=sb_secret_...

# Server-side only. How many proxies sit in front of the app, so the rate
# limiter knows how far into x-forwarded-for the real caller address is.
# Proxies append to that header, so the leftmost entry is whatever the caller
# typed — counting in from the right is what makes the address unforgeable.
#
# Vercel, Netlify, Fly, Render on their own: 1. Any of those behind Cloudflare
# as well: 2. Local development: leave it unset.
#
# Unset means there is no address worth trusting, so the per-address ceiling is
# switched off rather than fed a value the caller chose. The per-account ceiling
# still applies. Set this before going live — anonymous accounts are free to
# mint, so the per-address ceiling is the one that holds an attacker.
TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=1

# Safe to ship in the app bundle: Row Level Security is what protects the data,
# not the secrecy of these values.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...
